---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const setup = `mkdir mdbase-quickstart && cd mdbase-quickstart
npm init -y
npm install @mdbase-dev/sdk`;

const example = `import { connect, isMdbaseError, summarizeStatus } from "@mdbase-dev/sdk";
import { MemoryReplica } from "@mdbase-dev/sdk/testing";

// An in-memory stand-in for a replica. Writes stay pending until confirmAll().
const replica = new MemoryReplica({ confirmDelayMs: null });
replica.seed({
  path: "tasks/first.md",
  types: ["task"],
  frontmatter: { title: "Read the collection", status: "open" },
});

const db = await connect({
  connector: replica.connector(),
  app: { name: "dev.example.quickstart", version: "0.1.0" },
});

// A live query: a snapshot first, then a diff for every change.
const tasks = db.live({
  types: ["task"],
  order_by: [{ field: "file.path", direction: "asc" }],
});
await tasks.ready;
console.log(\`Tasks: \${tasks.records.map((r) => r.path).join(", ")}\`);

// Writes return at once with the optimistic result.
const created = await db.create({
  type: "task",
  path: "tasks/second.md",
  frontmatter: { title: "Update one record", status: "open" },
});
console.log(\`Created: \${created.records[0].path} (\${created.state})\`);
console.log(\`Status: \${summarizeStatus(await db.getStatus()).text}\`);

// Pass the record you read, so only the fields you change are sent.
const first = await db.get({ path: "tasks/first.md" });
const done = await db.update(first, { patch: { status: "done" } });

replica.confirmAll(); // The log accepts both writes.
const receipt = await done.confirmed;
console.log(\`Confirmed at position \${receipt.seq}\`);

// A whole-record check fails if the record changed since you read it.
try {
  const stale = await db.update(first, { patch: { status: "open" }, ifRevision: first.revision });
  await stale.confirmed;
} catch (e) {
  if (!isMdbaseError(e, "conflict")) throw e;
  console.log(\`Stale revision: \${e.code} (\${e.reason})\`);
}

console.log(\`Status: \${summarizeStatus(await db.getStatus()).text}\`);
console.log(\`Open tasks: \${tasks.records.filter((r) => r.frontmatter.get("status") === "open").length}\`);
tasks.close();
db.close();`;

const output = `Tasks: tasks/first.md
Created: tasks/second.md (pending)
Status: Synced through 1, 1 change waiting
Confirmed at position 3
Stale revision: conflict (revision)
Status: Synced through 3
Open tasks: 1`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart"
  description="Run a short script against an in-memory replica: read, watch, write and see a stale write refused."
  active="quickstart"
  headings={[
    { href: "#prerequisites", label: "Prerequisites" },
    { href: "#build", label: "Install the SDK" },
    { href: "#run", label: "Run the example" },
    { href: "#result", label: "Expected result" },
    { href: "#read", label: "What it shows" },
    { href: "#next", label: "Next steps" }
  ]}
>
  <p>
    This script needs no account, no service and no collection. It uses
    {" "}<code>MemoryReplica</code>, an in-memory replica from
    {" "}<code>@mdbase-dev/sdk/testing</code> that speaks the same protocol as a
    real one. Your code talks to it through the same
    {" "}<code>MdbaseClient</code> it would use with a real collection.
  </p>

  <h2 id="prerequisites">Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Node 20 or later.</li>
    <li>npm.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="build">1. Install the SDK</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={setup} language="sh" label="Terminal" />
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>The package is not on npm yet.</strong>
    <p>
      Until <code>@mdbase-dev/sdk</code> is published,
      {" "}<code>npm install</code> fails. This page will give the exact version
      once it is published.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="run">2. Run the example</h2>
  <p>
    Save this as <code>quickstart.mjs</code> and run
    {" "}<code>node quickstart.mjs</code>. It prints its results and exits.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={example} language="js" label="quickstart.mjs" />

  <h2 id="result">3. Check the result</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={output} language="text" label="Expected output" />

  <h2 id="read">4. What it shows</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Writes are optimistic.</strong> <code>create()</code> and
      {" "}<code>update()</code> return a <code>Write</code> straight away, in
      the <code>pending</code> state. Your reads and live queries already show
      the change. <code>write.confirmed</code> resolves when the collection’s
      log accepts it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Live queries stay current.</strong> <code>db.live()</code> keeps
      {" "}<code>records</code> up to date as writes land, so the count at the end
      already includes both changes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Frontmatter is a <code>Map</code>.</strong> Read fields with
      {" "}<code>record.frontmatter.get("status")</code>, or convert with
      {" "}<code>toPlain()</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stale writes are refused.</strong> With <code>ifRevision</code>,
      a write against an old revision fails with the error code
      {" "}<code>conflict</code> and reason <code>revision</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <code>MemoryReplica</code> is not the real replica. It applies patches
    blindly and has no query planner or merge. Use it for unit tests and demo
    modes, not to test merge behaviour.
  </p>

  <h2 id="next">5. Next steps</h2>
  <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
    <a class="button button--primary" href="/sdk/operations/">Read and write records</a>
    <a class="button" href="/sdk/offline-sync/">Pending writes and sync status</a>
    <a class="button" href="/sdk/testing/">Test with MemoryReplica</a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
